140 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R /E(Traditional blood bank management systems often rely on manual record-keeping, making it difficult to maintain accurate blood stock details, manage donor information, and identify the availability of specific blood groups during emergencies. These methods can lead to delays in retrieving records, errors in inventory tracking, and difficulties in matching donors with patients who require blood.)/Pg 12 0 R /K[ 0]>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 107 0 R /E(The Blood Bank Inventory and Repository System aims to develop a computerized solution using Java to store and manage donor details, blood group information, blood stock levels, and donation records. The system will enable users to add, search, update, and retrieve information efficiently, helping improve inventory management and support the timely availability of blood for patients in need.)/Pg 12 0 R /K[ 1]>>
endobj
